    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="71">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 71</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="71" corresp="#wit-g-a">⁊ beon þa heregeata swa fundene, swa hit mæðlic si:</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="71" corresp="#wit-a">⁊ beon þa heregeate, swa hit mæðlic sy:</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="71" corresp="#wit-q">Et sint releuationes ita inuentę, sicut modus sit:</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="71" corresp="#wit-b">And beon ða herigeata swa gefundene swa hit mæðlic sy.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a">And beon þa heregeata swa fundene, swa hit mæðlic si.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b">Heriots shall be fixed with due regard to the rank of the person for whom they are paid.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a">And a person’s tribute shall be assessed according to his status.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock">And heriots are to be so determined as befits the rank:</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">Und es seien die Hergewæte so festgesetzt, wie es standesgemäss ist:</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And let the heriots be fixed in such a way as befits [each one's] rank:</ab>
        <note type="editorial">‘fundene’ is a later bracketing in G and is missing in Ld.</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">swa fundene: omitted A</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">B adds rubric Eorles</note>
        <note type="translator" source="#rabin-doml">tribute: The heriot, that is, the military obligations, material, or financial support owed to the king. mancuses: A mancus is a gold coin worth roughly the equivalent of thirty pence.</note>
      </div>
    </body>
